    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nAI generated from a true bug:\n\nCython 3.3.0 miscompiles `not (x in <set> or add(x))` when add is a local bound to a set's `.add` method (`add = s.add`).\nIt optimises the call to `PySet_Add()`, then coerces the `(None)` return value to bool with the `PyLong` truthiness fast-path `__Pyx_PyLong_IsNonZero()` instead of `__Pyx_PyObject_IsTrue()`.\nThat reads `Py_SIZE(Py_None)` — UB, effectively \"truthy\" — so `x in s or add(x)` is always truthy and not (...) is always False.\n\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n```cython\ndef dedupe_via_local(seq):\n    seen = set()\n    seen_add = seen.add\n    return [x for x in seq if not (x in seen or seen_add(x))]\n\n# dedupe_via_local([\"a\", \"a\", \"b\"])\n#   Cython 3.2.9 -> ['a', 'b']   (correct)\n#   Cython 3.3.0 -> []           (wrong)\n```\n\n`seen.add(x)` inline compiles correctly; only the method-local form breaks.\nAlso breaks outside comprehensions (plain for loop). Reproduces at `-O0`, default directives, `CPython 3.14` / `x86-64` Linux.\n\nGenerated-C smoking gun (3.3.0)\n```\n__pyx_t_7 = PySet_Add(__pyx_v_seen, __pyx_v_x);          /* int status */\n__pyx_t_4 = __Pyx_Owned_Py_None(__pyx_t_7);              /* -> Py_None  */\nPy_ssize_t __pyx_temp = __Pyx_PyLong_IsNonZero(__pyx_t_4);   /* BUG: PyLong path on None */\n```\nvs. the correct dedupe_inline path: `__pyx_t_7 = (PySet_Add(...) != 0);`\n\nThe optimised call result node seems to retain an int/long result type from the `PySet_Add` status code, which then steers `CoerceToBooleanNode` into the `PyLong` fast path.\n\n\n### OS\nAny: Linux\n\n### Python version\n3.14.x\n\n### Cython version\n3.3.0\n\n### Additional context\n\nWe've applied this workaround to our cython code for now:\nhttps://github.com/Xpra-org/xpra/commit/316578aa3a233353a4d0d735474d64bfabcab522",
