            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Could you try it with the following PR branch? It might have an impact.\n\nAI generated: No. The patched Cython 3.3.0 still reproduces the Xpra failure:\n```\n  dedupe_via_local(...): got [], want ['a', 'b']\n  flags_via_local():     got [False, False, False], want [True, False, True]\n```\nCython PR #7923 fixes coercion when an expression result is discarded. In the Xpra workaround, `seen_add(x)` is used as a boolean operand, so `result_is_used` remains true and the new guard does not apply.\n\nThis is a separate Cython 3.3.0 bug and needs its own upstream fix.",
